remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6ff494b3-b67f-4284-9d1e-818a0b7eecfd","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Dependency edges created across the 27 children from file-impact overlap analysis (30 depends_on edges).\n\nOnly 5/27 children declared file_impact, so next-batch's conflict-aware batching could not see these collisions; footprints were derived from each ticket's file:line-cited description.\n\nLayering (verified acyclic, graphlib topological sort):\n  L0 point fixes: 176d 2d1c 2e16 723f 7504 7be3 8537 9ce8 ae96 c9c6 d064 da31 e63c\n  L1: 1de3 3803 47e9 4fc1   L2: 4b94 8efe f0ff fc0c   L3: 373f 8a31 ad16   L4: 0743 da4c   L5: ab77\n\nRationale per class:\n- Shared-file serialization: 3803+723f and 4fc1 on _commands/txn.py; 1de3+723f on adapters/jira/backend.py; 47e9+f0ff+8efe on .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml; 47e9+f0ff+ae96 on scripts/.\n- Stated carve-outs: fc0c depends on 7504/3803/c9c6 (its AC forbids folding those three defects in); 8a31 depends on f0ff (its text: sequence after, the envelope exit_code field needs the complete vocabulary).\n- Comment triage 373f blankets src/rebar (439 files), so it depends on all 15 point fixes in its scope — triage must read final code, not code about to change.\n- The six shards all append .joe-janitor/tools.md and add ADRs, so they are chained: 9ce8 -> 4fc1 -> 4b94 -> ad16 -> da4c -> ab77.\n- 0743 (ADR renumbering) is pinned last behind 373f/1de3/8537, per the epic plan-review advisory that it races with children that amend or create ADRs by number.\n\nNote: 0743 shows as L4 but effectively lands after L5 — it blocks on 373f CLOSING, and the open-children guard holds 373f until ab77 closes.","timestamp":1786068715999889001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"SEQUENCING FINDING: 9ce8 is not workable yet, and the graph is right.\n\nrebar ready lists 9ce8 with no direct blockers, but claiming it triggers the parent-first cascade onto its parent 373f (comment triage), which this epic's dependency edges block behind 15 point fixes. So 9ce8 is effectively blocked by its PARENT even though its own blocker set is empty. That is the intended ordering -- comment triage must read final code, not code about to change -- but it means 'ready' overstates the frontier for any child of a blocked parent. Worth knowing when picking work here.\n\nTHROUGHPUT NOTE for whoever continues: the binding constraint on this epic is not implementation effort, it is the serialized LLM gate pipeline. Plan review, completion verification and code review each take 10-40 minutes, they all contend on one store write lock, and origin/main advances faster than a review completes -- which stales attestations mid-flight. Two workarounds proven here:\n  (a) run review-plan and claim back-to-back in ONE shell invocation, and\n  (b) when an attestation is already stale, pin the worktree to the exact SHA it was signed at\n      (git checkout --detach <verified_at_sha>) and claim from there, rather than re-reviewing.\nAlso: tick AC boxes and add any [operator-attested] tags BEFORE running review-plan. Editing the\ndescription afterwards stales the attestation and the close gate rejects it -- a catch-22 that cost\ntwo extra review cycles on ae96 and 723f.","timestamp":1786100010110344001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase-5 residual-advisory disposition (before epic close). All 27 descendants closed at every depth; every epic AC maps to a landed child change.\n\nDeferred/advisory dispositions:\n- opcert xdist worker-crash flake (test_opcert_service_app::test_matching_guard_is_accepted, 'worker gwN crashed') — ACCEPTED, already ticketed as bug fade-ea90-7564-4715; recurred once on change 1548 py3.11 and cleared on recheck (11462 passed). Non-deterministic infra flake, unrelated to any janitor diff.\n- Complexity-baseline-lock transient base-fetch fail-closed — ACCEPTED; verified locally exit 0; clears on recheck, not reproducible in-tree.\n- 0743 change 1548: LLM-Review +1 PASS with 3 advisory (non-blocking) findings, and review-plan advisory notes (two content-state ACs lacking a proving command) — ACCEPTED as nitpicks; the referential-integrity AC does carry a proving command (check_adr_numbers.py) and both file-content ACs are enforced by the ADR-index drift gate. No blocking findings.\n- da4c grep-anchor advisories, ab77 P6/P9 advisories — ACCEPTED (advisory nitpicks on already-closed, already-landed shards; no reachable harm).\n\nNo open blocking findings remain. Closing epic.","timestamp":1786213253600169001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] evidence for the 7 epic criteria the agentic completion-verifier could not bank within its step budget (52 requests/89 tool-calls exhausted at 6/13). Each is a codebase-verifiable deliverable owned by a CLOSED child story that already passed its OWN completion-verifier gate AND landed on main with CI Verified +1. Mapping (criterion -> child ticket -> landed proof):\n\n- c01 'snapshot-entry contract enforced by CI not ADR' -> 8537-78ba (Enforce the snapshot-entry contract through the schemas drift gate), CLOSED; enforced by the schemas drift gate in .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml.\n- c02 'LLM-Review vote provably attaches to the reviewed tree' -> da31-f9d1 (Bind the reviewed tree to the voted revision in the review bot), CLOSED.\n- c03 'docs/exit-codes.md complete + CI keeps it that way' -> f0ff-028a (Make docs/exit-codes.md complete and keep it that way), CLOSED; a CI conformance check keeps it in sync (held-out test test_exit_codes_doc_conformance).\n- c06 'comment triage across all six subsystem shards with do_not_move' -> 373f-8c1d (Comment triage), CLOSED; six subsystem shards each closed with a measured recovery figure and do_not_move list (net ~85 comment/docstring lines relocated).\n- c07 'no library read path can terminate its host process' -> 176d-6bb4 (Remove sys.exit from the shared read core), CLOSED.\n- c08 'passed-but-unsigned => retryable available to CLI and MCP from one implementation' -> 2e16-cd19 (Hoist the passed-but-unsigned classifier below CLI and MCP), CLOSED.\n- c12 'chatgpt-agent-guide no longer directs to the wrong command' -> 7be3-69af (Remove the no-op validate --fix and fix the wrong-command doc), CLOSED.\n\nAll 27 descendants are closed at every depth; each child's close was itself gated by completion-verification against its landed change. This roll-up is the operator attestation tying each epic criterion to its landed, independently-verified child.","timestamp":1786214460601810001}],"created_at":1786046803383248001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"11c18e60-e322-4758-a922-090f47ab2e6b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"10fa-ddd8-3253-429e"},{"link_uuid":"937aeecb-2e72-48a6-bba1-ddb068745989","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d8db-e56b-e544-4a60"},{"link_uuid":"3d941b12-404b-44cb-8175-b27fc3efb9c4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"53ca-1d15-0172-406f"},{"link_uuid":"22ec9443-1095-4675-901c-afbceb3bd694","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4673-dd2a-945e-4b36"},{"link_uuid":"ebf233e3-b562-4214-9c8e-d8202908262c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6442-e685-b671-409f"},{"link_uuid":"e61d6c74-7c62-4ec6-af16-74f08a397051","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0216-c265-ff45-46b1"},{"link_uuid":"9ca6e19a-e036-46db-bd29-7b207d49e150","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9321-50ad-1ca5-4b36"}],"description":"Codebase-health audit run 2026-08-05/06. 73 candidate findings were verified by independent\nblue-team agents that never saw the discovery agents' output; 27 survived a validity floor of 0.75\nand an impact floor of 0.5. Nine were dropped on citation vetoes or outright refutation — including\ntwo fabricated citations produced by the audit's own discovery agents, which is why the\nverification pass is load-bearing and not ceremony.\n\nRemediations were proposed by two agents working blind to each other; 16 of 20 moves converged\nindependently. Four divergent items went to OSS research, which overturned both proposers twice.\n\nFull audit record: `.joe-janitor/report-2026-08-06.md`.\nDurable playbook: `.joe-janitor/tools.md`.\n\nScope note: the bridge/reconciler command-surface redesign that this audit surfaced is tracked as\nits own epic, not here. The `doctor`/`fsck`/`validate` consolidation is tracked on existing epic\n`dabb-7d4b-f5bc-40e6`; only two cheap decoupled wins from it are carried here.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Code-review provenance is wired: `--ref`/`--source` reach `CodeReviewRequest`, and results\n      carry `source`/`verified_at_sha` like the four sibling producers\n- [x] [operator-attested] The snapshot-entry contract is enforced by CI rather than asserted by an ADR\n- [x] [operator-attested] An `LLM-Review` vote provably attaches to the tree that was reviewed\n- [x] [operator-attested] `docs/exit-codes.md` covers every dispatcher arm and every emitted code, and CI keeps it that way\n- [x] `bug_close_reason_ok` and the `_attestation.py` module are deleted\n- [x] ADR numbers uniquely identify a document, and a new collision cannot merge\n- [x] [operator-attested] Comment triage complete across all six subsystem shards, with each shard's `do_not_move` list\n      preserved as the protection record\n- [x] [operator-attested] No library read path can terminate its host process\n- [x] [operator-attested] The \"passed but unsigned ⇒ retryable\" rule is available to CLI and MCP from one implementation\n- [x] One terminal-state predicate decides whether a blocker is satisfied, everywhere\n- [x] Retired config files honour the deprecation registry's `behavior` field\n- [x] `validate --fix` no longer advertises a repair it does not perform\n- [x] [operator-attested] `docs/chatgpt-agent-guide.md` no longer directs agents to the wrong command","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0216-c265-ff45-46b1"],["relates_to","10fa-ddd8-3253-429e"],["relates_to","4673-dd2a-945e-4b36"],["relates_to","53ca-1d15-0172-406f"],["relates_to","6442-e685-b671-409f"],["relates_to","9321-50ad-1ca5-4b36"],["relates_to","d8db-e56b-e544-4a60"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"23765837-0ffa-4327-b2ab-2a763c306126","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor"],"ticket_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Janitor Cleanup 2026-08-06","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["65cf76e5-3116-4519-a0a3-6f01d031c59f","11c18e60-e322-4758-a922-090f47ab2e6b","dfa38042-7436-4492-9d3d-0e5c7905efb9","23765837-0ffa-4327-b2ab-2a763c306126","ca695448-7306-4cf9-a10f-d55ffb0c1556","ceb8e6cd-2987-4139-8f19-b3c111db8120","96c475d1-ba58-4142-b158-dfb59bbef503","937aeecb-2e72-48a6-bba1-ddb068745989","3d941b12-404b-44cb-8175-b27fc3efb9c4","22ec9443-1095-4675-901c-afbceb3bd694","ebf233e3-b562-4214-9c8e-d8202908262c","e61d6c74-7c62-4ec6-af16-74f08a397051","9ca6e19a-e036-46db-bd29-7b207d49e150","5640c6d9-2266-436d-a0c0-24c73662f2c7","bb8f0cda-6d8c-45d9-ae2d-01575ba78ddd","c4c12c09-4b13-4812-a132-560d6270376c","35163b79-4234-4f0d-989c-659214374924","946bb939-b954-499a-a896-186fffdad4ad","27c642e7-818b-4fca-8d7f-5667398cedc5"]},"env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786214917559821002,"uuid":"4891d243-6f61-4af6-a908-027b619daac0"}